╭───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── ✅ Agent Final Answer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  Agent: Research Specialist                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  Final Answer:                                                                                                                                  │
│  - Perovskite–silicon tandem solar cells reached high-certified efficiencies in the mid-30s by 2025. The record stood at about 34.85%           │
│  certified by NREL (LONGi), achieved in late 2024, with 2025 reports continuing to push beyond the 34% mark and hinting at progress toward the  │
│  35% range in lab demonstrations.                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Tandem solar cells started moving from research into early commercialization in 2025. Oxford Photovoltaics shipped 24.5% efficient           │
│  perovskite–silicon tandem modules in late 2024, and 2025 developments saw ongoing scale-up and deployment efforts for tandem modules in pilot  │
│  production settings.                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - End-of-life solar PV recycling is evolving into a near-term business and policy focus. By 2025, Europe and other regions were expanding PV   │
│  recycling programs and regulatory frameworks; some studies estimated that with a 95% recycling yield, about 27,000 to 37,500 tons of silver    │
│  could be recovered from PV modules installed between 2000 and 2025.                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Building-integrated photovoltaics (BIPV) continued to grow as a major solar market segment. In 2025, the BIPV market was a                   │
│  multi-billion-dollar sector with Europe accounting for roughly 41.8% of demand (and APAC also a large contributor, cited at around 40–41% in   │
│  various analyses), driven by integration into roofs, façades, and shading devices.                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Solar windows and transparent photovoltaics made notable progress, though practical efficiencies remain modest in real-world use. By 2025,   │
│  lab records for transparent or semi-transparent PV approached 12% efficiency, while commercially deployed “solar windows” typically delivered  │
│  around 1–3% power conversion, reflecting a large gap between lab potential and ready-for-market products.                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
