│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  Agent: Research Specialist                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  Final Answer:                                                                                                                                  │
│  - Global solar PV market size in 2025 is already in the hundreds of billions of USD, with estimates ranging from about $368.7B (Grand View     │
│  Research) to about $502.8B (Fortune Business Insights) in 2025. Both sources project continued rapid growth into the late 2020s/early 2030s,   │
│  with forecasts implying roughly $800B–$1.5T scale by the end of the decade (CAGRs typically in the high single digits to low double digits).   │
│  (Sources include Grand View Research and Fortune Business Insights.)                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Building‑integrated photovoltaics (BIPV) remains a multi‑billion‑dollar segment in 2025, with Europe accounting for roughly 40% of BIPV      │
│  revenue and APAC around 40–41%. The European share and regional dynamics line up with ongoing policy support and demand, and the market is     │
│  projected to climb toward the tens of billions by 2030 (e.g., Europe ~40% share in 2025; Europe market size projection around $89.8B by        │
│  2030). (Sources include Precedence Research; Grand View Research; other BIPV market reports.)                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - PV recycling is a notable near‑term revenue opportunity: the 2025 solar panel recycling market was valued around $384–412 million across     │
│  sources, with multi‑billion forecasts downstream. Some projections extend to about $1.5 billion by 2034, while others show ~$610–$650 million  │
│  by 2033, reflecting strong growth driven by end‑of‑life PV management and policy.                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│    - 2025 value: about $384.4M (Grand View Research)                                                                                            │
│    - 2033 projection: about $609.7M (Grand View Research)                                                                                       │
│    - 2034 projection (alternative forecast): about $1,494M (Fortune Business Insights)                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Perovskite–silicon tandem solar cells show dramatic upside: the 2025 market for perovskite solar cells was around $0.46B, and forecasts      │
│  push to roughly $32.4B by 2033, a very high‑growth trajectory (~69% CAGR per some reports). This reflects anticipated efficiency gains and     │
│  rapid adoption in higher‑efficiency modules. (Sources include Grand View Research; Global Market Insights; others.)                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  - Tandem solar module market is in early but fast‑growing commercialization: 2025 tandem market size is reported around $39–$40 million, with  │
│  forecasts calling for very rapid expansion (e.g., CAGR ~41% through the early 2030s). Early module shipments (including pilot                  │
│  commercializations) in 2024–2025 set the stage for multi‑billion scale later in the decade. (Sources include Fortune Business Insights;        │
│  Strategic Market Research; other tandem market reports.)                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│  Note: Revenue outlook figures vary across research firms due to differing scopes (global PV vs. BIPV, modules vs. cells, end‑of‑life           │
│  recycling, etc.). The above pulls out representative 2025 baselines and clear growth trajectories from multiple credible sources.              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
